1
00:00:12,730 --> 00:00:15,550
♪I lean and gaze at misty waves afar♪

2
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:18,320
♪Tears fall on the ancient road
'neath the setting sun♪

3
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:21,460
♪One lone shadow on the cold river♪

4
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,910
♪In dreams, I return to the old window♪

5
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,670
♪Mountains stretch, the road home fades♪

6
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:32,030
♪A flute cries out, hooves hurry on♪

7
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,790
♪My heart adrift beneath a frosted moon♪

8
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:38,220
♪Drinking alone, I mourn our parting♪

9
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:40,050
♪Night turns cold, wind stirs the veil♪

10
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,760
♪Old robes recall forgotten days♪

11
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,570
♪Heart sore, a lone goose flies south♪

12
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:45,230
♪Where shall I send this letter?♪

13
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:47,760
♪Lost in thought through endless nights♪

14
00:00:47,770 --> 00:00:49,000
♪Love runs deep, dreams linger on♪

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,390
♪Only sorrow remains♪

16
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,340
♪A cup of wine, my shadow makes us two♪

17
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:54,980
♪Drunk and lost through flashing blades♪

18
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:56,870
♪I curse how swiftly the years pass by♪

19
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:58,580
♪The wandering road goes on♪

20
00:00:58,590 --> 00:01:01,020
♪Desolate, time frosts my youthful hair♪

21
00:01:01,030 --> 00:01:02,340
♪Through the years, love still burns♪

22
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:04,530
♪A thousand tears fall♪

23
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,030
♪Worlds apart, tears stain my sleeves♪

24
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:11,300
♪Old dreams haunt my heart,
tears cloud my eyes♪

25
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,340
♪Heartbroken, soul-worn,
pain won't fade♪

26
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:14,820
♪Moonlight westward, the night drags on♪

27
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:17,920
♪The years have left their scars♪

28
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:21,280
♪Autumn winds sweep leaves;
shadows pair♪

29
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:24,590
♪The past fades like smoke;
tears fall♪

30
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:26,820
♪My heart lies broken♪

31
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:30,150
♪Lost in thought through endless nights♪

32
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:34,980
[Love Legend]

33
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:38,780
[Episode 9]

34
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,230
A blood-jade craftsman?

35
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Take them away.

36
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:46,950
Ruoming.

37
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:49,920
Sir.

38
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:51,280
Xiao Ruoming,

39
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,640
go to the Ministry of Works

40
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:53,920
and check if any craftsmen are missing.

41
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:54,840
Yes, sir.

42
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:58,230
That girl's father
was a blood-jade craftsman.

43
00:01:59,310 --> 00:02:01,350
Does that mean the killer

44
00:02:01,350 --> 00:02:02,350
is also targeting blood-jade craftsmen?

45
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:06,070
All blood-jade craftsmen
are registered with the court.

46
00:02:06,210 --> 00:02:07,430
Even their wives and children

47
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:08,630
must be officially registered.

48
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,380
Could he have been

49
00:02:10,390 --> 00:02:11,440
an illegal blood-jade craftsman?

50
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,330
Unlikely.

51
00:02:15,090 --> 00:02:16,630
The proprietor is the daughter
of a blood-jade craftsman.

52
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:18,280
What if she

53
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:20,590
put that red mark on Madam Xu

54
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,750
to set her up on purpose?

55
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:24,430
Maybe she didn't mean to.

56
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,590
No way.

57
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,060
That woman

58
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:28,240
is far too shrewd.

59
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:28,980
Enough.

60
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:30,710
She's just a merchant.

61
00:02:30,930 --> 00:02:31,800
How would she know that girl

62
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,750
was connected to a blood-jade craftsman?

63
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:34,960
Ruoming,

64
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,750
why are you so worked up?

65
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:39,000
I'm not.

66
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:45,560
Sir.

67
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,430
I'll go to the Ministry of Works now.

68
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:51,710
Sir.

69
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:52,800
I'll see what's wrong with him.

70
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:04,360
It's empty.

71
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:06,680
Sir,

72
00:03:06,850 --> 00:03:08,240
I don't think the proprietor left
on her own.

73
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:10,570
Could she have been taken too?

74
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:13,740
Traffickers only target

75
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:15,720
girls from poor families.

76
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:18,630
Proprietor Xiao has made a name
in Ghost Market.

77
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:19,840
She's not someone

78
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,000
ordinary people would dare cross.

79
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:22,330
Could it be

80
00:03:22,970 --> 00:03:23,810
an enemy came for her?

81
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:27,150
Sir.

82
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:29,100
No craftsmen are missing
from the Ministry's records.

83
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:30,610
Sir.

84
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:35,000
What happened here?

85
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:38,030
Why is it such a mess?

86
00:03:40,190 --> 00:03:41,520
Everything's been cleared out.

87
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:47,870
Sir.

88
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:52,120
What's wrong with Ruoming?

89
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:52,690
Sir,

90
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:54,310
do you think

91
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:56,630
Ruoming knows the proprietor well?

92
00:03:57,230 --> 00:03:58,980
He didn't look

93
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:00,750
quite right.

94
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:03,910
The proprietor can't
have been gone long.

95
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,050
We should

96
00:04:05,330 --> 00:04:06,030
look for clues first.

97
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:10,840
Ruoming.

98
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,280
What's wrong with you today?

99
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:14,390
Nothing.

100
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:16,560
Are you and the proprietor

101
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,380
close?

102
00:04:17,870 --> 00:04:18,680
No.

103
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,600
I only know her

104
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:22,830
from buying info in Ghost Market.

105
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:23,920
Do you have any idea

106
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,040
how upset you looked

107
00:04:25,950 --> 00:04:27,240
in front of Lord Pei today?

108
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:28,270
I thought

109
00:04:28,270 --> 00:04:29,390
you two had some special bond.

110
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:31,240
What bond could I have with her?

111
00:04:33,510 --> 00:04:34,120
Right.

112
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:34,830
Chang'an.

113
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:36,800
I need to go out for a while.

114
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:37,970
Cover for me

115
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:39,670
with Lord Pei.

116
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:47,310
Sir.

117
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:49,160
Where's Xiao Ruoming?

118
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:49,920
He...

119
00:04:50,570 --> 00:04:51,480
He found a clue,

120
00:04:51,630 --> 00:04:53,030
so he went out.

121
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,030
What clue?

122
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,270
He didn't say.

123
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:56,720
But don't worry, sir.

124
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,040
If he finds anything,

125
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,190
he'll report to you right away.

126
00:05:01,610 --> 00:05:02,710
Sir.

127
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:03,750
Come look at this.

128
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,190
What is it?

129
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,310
These four portraits

130
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:11,270
show girls dressed exactly like

131
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:12,270
the portraits we saw

132
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:12,920
at the prefecture.

133
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,600
I think

134
00:05:15,310 --> 00:05:17,390
these girls are missing too.

135
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:19,000
Proprietor Xiao must've seen them.

136
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:24,190
Chang'an.

137
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:27,070
Bring Governor Liu here.

138
00:05:27,950 --> 00:05:28,750
Yes, sir.

139
00:05:33,270 --> 00:05:34,680
Speak, Lord Liu.

140
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,260
It's just you and me.

141
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:38,370
No need to hide anything now.

142
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:40,160
Lord Pei,

143
00:05:41,190 --> 00:05:42,720
you've seen the case files.

144
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:45,430
I have nothing else to tell you.

145
00:05:46,170 --> 00:05:47,360
That's not true.

146
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,230
Many people are missing,

147
00:05:49,230 --> 00:05:50,290
yet none of them were reported.

148
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,680
They're only lowly Wingless.

149
00:05:54,150 --> 00:05:55,210
No need to mind them.

150
00:05:57,670 --> 00:06:00,130
Some of them
concern His Majesty's safety.

151
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:03,330
If you won't talk,
I cannot save you.

152
00:06:03,630 --> 00:06:04,400
His Majesty?

153
00:06:06,310 --> 00:06:08,030
Lord Pei, did you notice

154
00:06:08,030 --> 00:06:09,360
their dates of birth?

155
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:11,160
Lord Pei,

156
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:12,240
that's all I can say.

157
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:14,630
I urge you to stop digging.

158
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,310
Across the capital,

159
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,240
apart from you,

160
00:06:17,750 --> 00:06:19,750
everyone else

161
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:21,310
turns a blind eye.

162
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,040
So you knew all along

163
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:23,920
where they went.

164
00:06:30,870 --> 00:06:32,920
So those young girls

165
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:35,480
were taken by palace nobles

166
00:06:36,070 --> 00:06:37,190
for their pleasure?

167
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,310
There is a feast in the capital

168
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:40,360
called the Blood Banquet.

169
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:41,750
They believe

170
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:42,950
the blood of young girls

171
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:43,950
can prolong life.

172
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:47,920
A cup of blood wine,

173
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,270
ten more years of life.

174
00:06:50,510 --> 00:06:51,240
Disgusting.

175
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:53,190
Shameless.

176
00:06:54,070 --> 00:06:54,870
Madam Xu,

177
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:56,600
when Yun Qi took you,

178
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,920
was it for a Blood Banquet too?

179
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,510
He deserves to die.

180
00:06:59,510 --> 00:07:00,510
Ji Chang'an.

181
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:02,600
Got a frog in your throat?

182
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,070
I'm just so angry.

183
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:11,400
What's so special

184
00:07:11,830 --> 00:07:13,040
about these girls' birth dates?

185
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:14,800
If only Lu were here.

186
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:15,560
He'd know.

187
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:16,950
Sir,

188
00:07:16,950 --> 00:07:18,950
why don't we copy

189
00:07:18,950 --> 00:07:20,040
all their birth dates

190
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,750
and ask a fortune-teller on the street?

191
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,040
Good idea.

192
00:07:24,010 --> 00:07:24,370
All right.

193
00:07:24,970 --> 00:07:25,420
Go.

194
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:26,310
Yes, sir.

195
00:07:28,790 --> 00:07:29,560
Wait.

196
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:31,900
Bring Xiao Ruoming back.

197
00:07:32,150 --> 00:07:33,160
Has he forgotten the rules?

198
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:34,280
I will.

199
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,310
- Brother Xiao.
- Brother Xiao.

200
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,360
Has Ruoli been here lately?

201
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:47,680
She hasn't come for days.

202
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:49,450
Has anyone suspicious come
looking for her?

203
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:51,360
No.

204
00:07:51,370 --> 00:07:53,360
Just people buying things from her.

205
00:07:53,770 --> 00:07:54,600
Wait.

206
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,830
That's not right.

207
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:58,770
Someone did come a few days ago.

208
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:00,120
He wore a black robe

209
00:08:00,690 --> 00:08:01,720
and

210
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:04,190
a really scary mask.

211
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:05,630
And on his waist,

212
00:08:05,630 --> 00:08:07,230
he had a dead fish.

213
00:08:07,730 --> 00:08:08,390
A dead fish?

214
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:11,750
Did you see what he came for?

215
00:08:12,250 --> 00:08:14,920
He drove everyone out.

216
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:17,580
Then I heard Ruoli tell him

217
00:08:17,590 --> 00:08:18,700
to get out.

218
00:08:18,930 --> 00:08:20,030
When she comes back,

219
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,260
tell her to find me right away.

220
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,630
It's dangerous out there lately.

221
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,600
Don't go out begging.

222
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,550
- Thank you, Brother Xiao.
- Thank you.

223
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:36,030
Take good care of yourselves.

224
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:37,670
- Goodbye, Brother Xiao.
- Goodbye.

225
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:47,320
My belly hurts.

226
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:47,990
Stop right there.

227
00:08:48,970 --> 00:08:50,000
Brother Xiao.

228
00:08:52,270 --> 00:08:53,780
Please save Xiaoyu.

229
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,440
Xiaoyu.

230
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,720
The man in black only showed his eyes.

231
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:05,080
They looked vicious.

232
00:09:05,550 --> 00:09:06,870
At his waist

233
00:09:06,870 --> 00:09:07,960
was a silver fish pendant.

234
00:09:08,570 --> 00:09:10,000
The fish had dead-looking eyes.

235
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:10,720
All white.

236
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:13,200
Did it look like this?

237
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:14,380
Yes.

238
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:16,640
Sir.

239
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,020
I don't understand.

240
00:09:23,790 --> 00:09:25,360
Why would they take a little beggar?

241
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:27,120
Weren't they only taking girls before?

242
00:09:27,290 --> 00:09:29,050
He took my little sister.

243
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:29,830
Your sister?

244
00:09:30,650 --> 00:09:31,320
A girl?

245
00:09:31,850 --> 00:09:33,570
She's like a little sister to me.

246
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:35,720
We always play together.

247
00:09:36,170 --> 00:09:36,790
How old is she?

248
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:38,390
What year and month was she born?

249
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:38,950
And at what hour?

250
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:40,450
She was born

251
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:41,970
in the Yichou year,

252
00:09:42,430 --> 00:09:43,520
in the Yimao month,

253
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,000
on the Yichou day,

254
00:09:45,090 --> 00:09:46,390
at the Yimao hour.

255
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:49,480
How do you recall it so clearly?

256
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:50,960
Half a month ago,

257
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:53,550
Ruoli asked for her birth details.

258
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,200
Sir, I checked.

259
00:09:55,650 --> 00:09:57,480
Those girls were all born

260
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:59,420
in a yin year, month, hour, and day.

261
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,740
They have pure-yin constitutions.

262
00:10:01,430 --> 00:10:02,630
The missing girl

263
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:03,720
is a pure-yin girl.

264
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:06,390
I was born in a yin year too.

265
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:09,360
Your blood is of pure yin.

266
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:11,440
Sacrificing your blood

267
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:14,000
will keep our family prosperous forever.

268
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,910
Could they be like me?

269
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,080
Were they all taken to be sacrificed?

270
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:17,960
Yes.

271
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:19,450
And no.

272
00:10:20,150 --> 00:10:20,960
What do you mean?

273
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,070
You share their birth hour,

274
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,390
but not their constitution.

275
00:10:24,910 --> 00:10:26,480
They died from ordinary blades,

276
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:28,200
while you survived
seven blood-jade hairpins.

277
00:10:29,030 --> 00:10:30,960
My blood is more useful?

278
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:32,240
Come on.

279
00:10:32,610 --> 00:10:33,670
I'll take you somewhere.

280
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:38,660
[Guard Infirmary]

281
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:39,360
Sir,

282
00:10:39,650 --> 00:10:40,500
what is this place?

283
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:43,150
Injured Fengyi Guards

284
00:10:43,490 --> 00:10:44,630
are sent here for treatment.

285
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,240
But once they're sent here,

286
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,290
it also means

287
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:48,690
they can never return
to the Fengyi Bureau.

288
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:49,750
Why?

289
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,870
The Fengyi Guard handles

290
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,630
the most dangerous

291
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:54,790
and secretive missions of any agency.

292
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:57,150
So...

293
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:00,110
- Their wounds are the worst.
- Sir.

294
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:01,980
Can't they recover?

295
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,000
Sir.

296
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:05,750
Sir.

297
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,550
He was wounded by a blood-jade weapon

298
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,000
while fighting the rebels.

299
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:19,320
It's been two years,

300
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:20,740
and the wound still hasn't healed.

301
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:22,840
Two years?

302
00:11:23,870 --> 00:11:24,580
Sir.

303
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:25,630
It doesn't hurt anymore.

304
00:11:25,860 --> 00:11:26,510
Really.

305
00:11:26,770 --> 00:11:27,770
I want to return to the Fengyi Bureau.

306
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,270
Rest and recover first.

307
00:11:32,050 --> 00:11:32,780
Yes, sir.

308
00:11:35,310 --> 00:11:36,960
Weapons made of blood jade

309
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:38,270
are extremely deadly.

310
00:11:38,730 --> 00:11:40,110
The ore is corrosive.

311
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:42,440
Once you're cut by a blood-jade weapon,

312
00:11:42,590 --> 00:11:43,840
the wound is corroded

313
00:11:44,310 --> 00:11:45,120
and rarely heals.

314
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,840
But my wounds healed quickly.

315
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,910
Are all the Yuns like this?

316
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:52,510
Sir,

317
00:11:52,970 --> 00:11:54,480
do you know something?

318
00:11:58,600 --> 00:11:59,480
I trust you.

319
00:11:59,630 --> 00:12:00,670
If you find out anything,

320
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:01,630
please tell me.

321
00:12:04,130 --> 00:12:04,570
All right.

322
00:12:05,650 --> 00:12:06,270
Thank you.

323
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:07,760
Sir,

324
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,270
could you

325
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,520
do me one more little favor?

326
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:12,690
Don't push it.

327
00:12:13,870 --> 00:12:14,870
You're so kind, sir.

328
00:12:14,950 --> 00:12:15,890
I know you'll help me.

329
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,270
This favor

330
00:12:32,270 --> 00:12:33,240
is shopping?

331
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:34,150
Sir,

332
00:12:34,150 --> 00:12:35,150
just lend me some money.

333
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:35,960
I'll choose it myself.

334
00:12:41,750 --> 00:12:43,630
Making more incense-beads?

335
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:45,440
Ji Chang'an has but one waist.

336
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:46,910
You will wear him out.

337
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:48,120
Not for Chang'an.

338
00:12:50,630 --> 00:12:52,510
I don't need it either.

339
00:12:52,510 --> 00:12:53,390
If you have such energy,

340
00:12:53,390 --> 00:12:55,150
use it to prepare for the selection.

341
00:12:55,150 --> 00:12:56,390
Not for you either.

342
00:12:56,390 --> 00:12:57,480
Then who?

343
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,550
Lu Li?

344
00:12:58,550 --> 00:12:59,360
Xiao Ruoming?

345
00:13:00,590 --> 00:13:01,260
It's a secret.

346
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:02,440
Sir,

347
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:03,440
where can I buy a pigeon?

348
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,150
No pigeons are allowed

349
00:13:05,150 --> 00:13:06,550
in the Fengyi Bureau.

350
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:08,360
I'm telling you,

351
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:09,550
last time, over there,

352
00:13:09,550 --> 00:13:10,390
I used that move you taught me.

353
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:11,150
Two punches, just like that.

354
00:13:11,150 --> 00:13:11,510
Stop it.

355
00:13:19,020 --> 00:13:19,630
- Sir.
- Sir.

356
00:13:20,210 --> 00:13:21,080
These are tonics.

357
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:23,030
Take them to those young beggars

358
00:13:23,030 --> 00:13:24,080
and the little girl.

359
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:25,120
Yes.

360
00:13:26,250 --> 00:13:27,720
You really are a kind official.

361
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,440
They're still useful.

362
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:32,000
They need to regain their strength

363
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,000
before we can question them.

364
00:13:33,890 --> 00:13:34,550
Go.

365
00:13:35,390 --> 00:13:36,240
Madam Xu,

366
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:36,960
I'll walk you back to your room.

367
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:38,150
Ji Chang'an.

368
00:13:38,630 --> 00:13:39,910
Deliver the medicine.

369
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:41,600
Yes, sir.

370
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:52,390
Sir.

371
00:13:52,530 --> 00:13:53,960
I'll go back to my room now.

372
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,120
Xiao Ruoming.

373
00:14:03,550 --> 00:14:05,360
Still hiding the truth from me?

374
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,630
What is your relationship

375
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:09,480
with the proprietor?

376
00:14:10,630 --> 00:14:11,440
Sir,

377
00:14:12,750 --> 00:14:14,270
I swear on my life

378
00:14:14,550 --> 00:14:16,030
the proprietor would never hurt anyone.

379
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,390
Fine.

380
00:14:19,030 --> 00:14:21,080
I'm giving you one last chance.

381
00:14:24,390 --> 00:14:25,790
Go take twenty lashes.

382
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:33,700
Yes, sir.

383
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:39,100
[Fengyi Bureau]

384
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,840
Why not just tell the truth?

385
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,670
There's nothing wrong

386
00:14:44,670 --> 00:14:45,600
with liking a girl.

387
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:47,960
None of your concern.

388
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:50,200
I remember you told me

389
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:52,440
you are

390
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,480
an only child

391
00:14:53,750 --> 00:14:54,790
with no parents.

392
00:14:55,630 --> 00:14:56,720
I know.

393
00:14:57,030 --> 00:14:58,080
She's your mother.

394
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,270
Why else would you protect her so much?

395
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,200
How can you be so absurd?

396
00:15:04,150 --> 00:15:06,000
No wonder Lord Pei said
you belong in a theater troupe.

397
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,080
I'm not going anywhere.

398
00:15:09,030 --> 00:15:10,030
I'm staying

399
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,840
at the Fengyi Bureau for life.

400
00:15:12,390 --> 00:15:14,000
When Lord Pei gets promoted,

401
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,030
I'll become Chief Commander.

402
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:17,630
Chang'an.

403
00:15:18,790 --> 00:15:19,810
Go get some rest.

404
00:15:21,390 --> 00:15:22,390
The selection

405
00:15:22,390 --> 00:15:23,220
is coming up,

406
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:26,120
and the missing-girls case
is still unsolved.

407
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:27,840
Go get some rest.

408
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:29,320
All right. I'm going.

409
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:41,140
[Fengyi Guard Selection Combat Trial]

410
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:44,840
The Crown Prince arrives.

411
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,460
Everyone, rise.

412
00:16:22,550 --> 00:16:23,750
I observe for His Majesty.

413
00:16:23,750 --> 00:16:25,030
I will offer no judgment.

414
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:26,440
Lord Pei, choose as you see fit.

415
00:16:27,490 --> 00:16:28,050
Yes, Your Highness.

416
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:36,150
Let the selection begin.

417
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:38,510
Put on your masks.

418
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,000
Lord Pei,

419
00:16:44,550 --> 00:16:46,150
why must they all wear masks?

420
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,080
Your Highness,

421
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:49,120
every selection

422
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,440
brings people who try

423
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:51,920
to plant their own men
in the Fengyi Bureau.

424
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,030
They bribe candidates

425
00:16:53,030 --> 00:16:54,750
to deliberately lose
during the written exam.

426
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:56,750
With everyone masked,

427
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:57,870
no one knows who's who.

428
00:16:58,030 --> 00:16:59,840
So they won't know
who they're supposed to lose to.

429
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:06,640
First round.

430
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:07,680
Combat trial.

431
00:17:09,770 --> 00:17:11,110
During the trial,

432
00:17:11,110 --> 00:17:12,480
stop once you've made your point.

433
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:13,790
No killing.

434
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,680
No sneak attacks.

435
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,920
No poison.

436
00:17:19,110 --> 00:17:20,200
Combat trial,

437
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,160
begin.

438
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:29,720
Ruoming.

439
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,320
Bring the brazier.

440
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:39,720
Pei Zhao,

441
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,110
what is this about?

442
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,200
By His Majesty's decree,

443
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,480
those selected this year

444
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,510
will form the Fengyi Bureau's

445
00:17:45,510 --> 00:17:46,350
first Shadow Guard.

446
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:47,310
Their faces,

447
00:17:47,310 --> 00:17:48,550
identities, and names

448
00:17:48,550 --> 00:17:50,590
will cease to exist from this moment on.

449
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:54,440
Why have I

450
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:56,310
never heard Father mention this?

451
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,070
After the selection,

452
00:17:58,070 --> 00:17:59,790
a group of recruits will be assigned

453
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:01,110
as the Crown Prince's secret guards.

454
00:18:01,110 --> 00:18:02,440
They will answer only to Your Highness.

455
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:03,270
Their identities

456
00:18:03,270 --> 00:18:05,270
will be known only to you.

457
00:18:05,270 --> 00:18:06,440
Everything we're doing today

458
00:18:06,610 --> 00:18:08,150
is to prevent anyone

459
00:18:08,150 --> 00:18:10,140
from planting spies at your side.

460
00:18:23,350 --> 00:18:26,160
♪A cold blade gleams by the window♪

461
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:30,970
♪Candle tears harden into frost♪

462
00:18:32,290 --> 00:18:34,030
♪Moon shadows flicker and sway♪

463
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:38,970
♪A wisp of longing haunts the air♪

464
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:43,800
♪A lone boat rests on the misty river♪

465
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:50,030
♪That promise lies sealed with my sword♪

466
00:18:50,350 --> 00:18:58,380
♪I turn to find the world in snow♪

467
00:18:58,650 --> 00:19:07,270
♪Fated destiny ties from bygone life♪

468
00:19:07,270 --> 00:19:15,940
♪Longing for one beloved flows on♪

469
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:25,190
♪I can't let go of the verses lost
across this vast land♪

470
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:34,110
♪Yet I let go of that fleeting light
within your eyes♪
